WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.220 --> 00:00:08.160
We saw that the gravitational force is the attractive

00:00:08.160 --> 00:00:11.500
force between any two objects with non-zero mass

00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:14.400
seperated by a distance.

00:00:14.480 --> 00:00:16.780
So does the Apple fall towards the Earth

00:00:16.780 --> 00:00:19.220
or does the Earth move towards the Apple?

00:00:19.380 --> 00:00:21.260
Or do both move towards each other?

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:24.220
It’s actually simple logic!

00:00:24.220 --> 00:00:28.860
This is the Earth, and say this minuscule object is an Apple.

00:00:28.980 --> 00:00:32.040
Based on what we learnt about the gravitational force,

00:00:32.040 --> 00:00:36.140
both apply an equal force to attract the other object towards itself.

00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:41.060
So if the forces are equal which one will accelerate more?

00:00:41.340 --> 00:00:43.200
Based on the Newton’s second law,

00:00:43.420 --> 00:00:45.500
we know that the force applied is the product

00:00:45.500 --> 00:00:47.500
of mass and acceleration.

00:00:47.880 --> 00:00:51.780
So the acceleration will equal ‘Force over the mass’.

00:00:52.400 --> 00:00:55.640
The acceleration is inversely proportional to the mass.

00:00:56.000 --> 00:00:58.920
If the mass is more, the acceleration will be lesser.

00:00:59.380 --> 00:01:02.720
As the mass of the Earth is MUCH MUCH MUCH more

00:01:02.720 --> 00:01:04.200
than the mass of the Apple,

00:01:04.280 --> 00:01:07.020
It is the Apple that accelerates towards the Earth

00:01:07.040 --> 00:01:09.300
and not the other way around.

00:01:09.560 --> 00:01:11.260
Hope that makes it clear.

00:01:11.700 --> 00:01:15.180
Now the question is ‘how do we quantify this force?’

00:01:15.300 --> 00:01:18.080
To understand this, we need to understand

00:01:18.080 --> 00:01:19.480
a simple concept!

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:21.960
And this simple concept is called

00:01:21.960 --> 00:01:24.640
the Universal law of Gravitation.

00:01:25.480 --> 00:01:27.880
Say there are two objects A and B

00:01:27.880 --> 00:01:30.160
separated by a distance ‘d’.

00:01:30.380 --> 00:01:33.180
The distance between the centres is considered the

00:01:33.180 --> 00:01:34.260
distance between the 2

00:01:34.260 --> 00:01:36.860
objects and not this distance.

00:01:37.060 --> 00:01:39.960
Assume that the mass of object A is ‘m1’

00:01:39.960 --> 00:01:42.680
and that of object B is ‘m2’.

00:01:43.240 --> 00:01:46.055
As object A is bigger, let’s assume

00:01:46.060 --> 00:01:48.180
'm1' to be bigger than 'm2'.

00:01:48.860 --> 00:01:52.040
The Universal law of gravitation says that,

00:01:52.040 --> 00:01:55.335
‘Every object in the universe attracts every object

00:01:55.335 --> 00:01:58.055
with a force which is DIRECTLY proportional

00:01:58.060 --> 00:02:00.400
to the product of their masses and

00:02:00.400 --> 00:02:01.940
INVERSELY proportional

00:02:01.940 --> 00:02:04.260
to the SQUARE of the distance between them’.

00:02:04.540 --> 00:02:05.760
Let me repeat.

00:02:06.100 --> 00:02:08.380
The force is Directly proportional

00:02:08.380 --> 00:02:10.340
to the PRODUCT of their masses

00:02:10.340 --> 00:02:13.475
and INVERSELY proportional to the SQUARE of the

00:02:13.475 --> 00:02:14.535
distance between them.

00:02:14.880 --> 00:02:18.660
With this data, we can write it mathematically like this.

00:02:19.060 --> 00:02:22.055
So if the mass of any of the objects increases,

00:02:22.055 --> 00:02:25.425
the gravitational force will have more magnitude.

00:02:25.540 --> 00:02:28.280
And more the distance between the two objects,

00:02:28.280 --> 00:02:30.620
the lesser will the gravitational force!

00:02:30.940 --> 00:02:33.900
Directly proportional to the product of the masses,

00:02:33.900 --> 00:02:35.540
and inversely proportional

00:02:35.540 --> 00:02:38.220
to the square of the distance between them.

00:02:38.680 --> 00:02:42.180
This can be written as F equals G times m1 one times

00:02:42.320 --> 00:02:44.220
m2 over 'd' squared.

00:02:45.020 --> 00:02:48.860
‘G’ here is the Constant of proportionality and is called

00:02:48.860 --> 00:02:51.500
the UNIVERSAL GRAVITAITONAL CONSTANT.

00:02:51.680 --> 00:02:54.600
The equation can be modified and written as

00:02:54.740 --> 00:02:58.960
G equals ‘F times d squared' over ‘m1 times m2’.

00:02:59.860 --> 00:03:01.940
The value of ‘G’ was found out by

00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:05.140
Lord Henry Cavendish using a Torsion Balance.

00:03:06.640 --> 00:03:09.140
The universally accepted value of G is

00:03:09.140 --> 00:03:13.360
‘six point six seven three’ times ‘ten raised to negative 11’.

00:03:13.805 --> 00:03:15.795
What will be the units of G?

00:03:16.020 --> 00:03:17.540
Force is Newtons.

00:03:17.540 --> 00:03:21.320
As the distance is in meters, we have ‘meters squared’.

00:03:21.480 --> 00:03:23.880
And as the mass is measured using kilograms,

00:03:23.900 --> 00:03:27.460
we multiply this with ‘kilograms raised to negative 2’.

00:03:28.140 --> 00:03:33.520
This is the value of the Universal gravitational constant!

